# Go sources are stored and checked out with LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF working
# copies while the blobs stay LF. gofmt emits LF, so it reports every one of
# those files as unformatted — fifteen of them, eleven thousand lines of
# phantom diff — and the one real formatting problem is invisible in the noise.
# Running `gofmt -w` to "fix" it rewrites line endings that Git then converts
# back on the next checkout.
*.go text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# The CI gate compares these byte for byte.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Program inputs and generated goldens.
*.xql text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
